From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenAI <noreply@openai.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tu: test conservative memory budget for FF7R on SD865

The current Turnip memory-budget query reports up to 90% of available
system memory (bounded by the advertised heap and GPU VA size). In the
captured FF7R OOM runs, large 128 MiB and 256 MiB requests failed while
DXVK's reported budget was near its current allocation total, and its
empty-pool reclaim pass reclaimed zero bytes.

For this isolated FF7R profile, report 75% of available system memory
instead. This is an experiment to make budget-aware clients react earlier
to unified-memory pressure; it does not cap real allocations, free memory,
or guarantee recovery. Keep the upstream 90% policy unchanged in all other
profiles and compare against the existing 512 KiB pipeline profile.

---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
@@ -1800,9 +1800,10 @@ tu_get_budget_memory(struct tu_physical_device *physical_device)
    /*
-    * Let's not incite the app to starve the system: report at most 90% of
+    * FF7R SD865 experiment: leave more headroom under unified-memory pressure.
+    * The upstream default remains 90% in all non-experimental profiles.
     * available system memory.
     */
-   uint64_t heap_available = sys_available * 9 / 10;
+   uint64_t heap_available = sys_available * 3 / 4;
    return MIN2(heap_size, heap_used + heap_available);
